WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.221
Can society be studied like

2
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:04.659
nature? Durkheim said yes.

3
00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:06.826
Weber said: not quite.

4
00:00:07.159 --> 00:00:08.158
In 1895,

5
00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:11.458
Durkheim said: treat social facts

6
00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:12.753
as things.

7
00:00:12.753 --> 00:00:14.361
External to individuals,

8
00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:16.285
and constraining them.

9
00:00:16.961 --> 00:00:19.303
Weber argued for verstehen,

10
00:00:19.303 --> 00:00:21.545
understanding the meaning people give

11
00:00:21.545 --> 00:00:23.131
to their actions.

12
00:00:23.819 --> 00:00:26.616
Interpretive sociologists put meaning before

13
00:00:26.616 --> 00:00:29.744
measurement. Critical theorists said science

14
00:00:29.744 --> 00:00:31.924
is never fully value-free.

15
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:33.452
Your turn.

16
00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:35.761
Whose advice is this?
